# Trial of Agony's ruling (CR 608.2b, 2024-09-20): if one of the two target creatures is an illegal target as it resolves, its controller
# "chooses" the remaining one and it is dealt 5 damage. On turn 3 Bot1 targets Bot2's Elvish Mystic and Memnite; in response Bot1's Lightning Bolt
# kills Memnite, then Trial of Agony resolves and Bot2 "chooses" the Mystic, the only legal target, which takes 5.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Mox Ruby
Trial of Agony
Lightning Bolt
Mountain x16

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Elvish Mystic
Memnite
Forest x17

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Elvish Mystic.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Memnite.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby#2.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Trial of Agony.Cast
Bot1.Target(Elvish Mystic; Memnite)
Bot1.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Memnite)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Choose(Elvish Mystic)
[Bot1.Main2]
? Bot2.Graveyard = Elvish Mystic; Memnite

[Expect]
Bot2.Battlefield.Count = 1
Bot1.Graveyard = Trial of Agony; Lightning Bolt
